id: pm-gh1571
title: "GH-1571: allow projection of active extension item fields across read surfaces"
description: "SDK get/list/search projection validation now includes active extension registerItemFields names alongside runtime schema metadata. Typed scalar/container values and valid custom selectors survive compact SDK, CLI and native action reads, while disabled or unknown fields remain refused. Source report and original intake are preserved in the body and immutable history."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[4]: extensions,github,projection,sdk
created_at: "2026-10-24T07:04:53.631Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-24T11:16:20.890Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-24T11:16:20.204Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-24T11:16:20.204Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 240
acceptance_criteria: Add a sandbox reproduction against the active runtime registry covering SDK and CLI get/list/search.; Preserve numeric and other supported declared field values and reject truly unknown names without silently dropping requested fields.; Keep CLI and MCP adapters on shared SDK projection contracts and update discovery and recovery where needed.; Prove extension activation isolation and built-in projection compatibility through meaningful regression tests and linked evidence.
parent: pm-ugqx
risk: medium
confidence: medium
severity: medium
environment: "Reporter: published npm CLI and SDK 2026.10.24 in a plain temporary directory without git; local schema-capability extension registers optional numeric probe_score."
repro_steps: "Use the attached source reproduction in the item body: init a temporary tracker; activate a local registerItemFields extension; create probe_score=3; compare full get with projected SDK get and CLI get/list/search."
resolution: "Get/list/search validate active registerItemFields selectors, retain declared values and recovery selectors, and isolate disabled registrations. The regression fixture uses literal extension JavaScript, eliminating CodeQL51 construction without suppressions."
expected_result: "Extensions can select domain fields through all read transports, with typed recovery and registration isolation, and the regression test avoids generated code interpolation."
actual_result: Both regression cases pass after the literal fixture update; strict lint and all typechecking projects pass. The prior accepted source passes14 hosted platform legs and exact100percent merged coverage. New final-head CodeQL and required CI run after this reviewed push.
affected_version: 2026.10.24
component: SDK read projection and extension field registry
customer_impact: Extension packages must fetch full rows to recover requested domain fields; reporter measured two calls and about 1600 tokens to read one scalar.
